    bottomLine: "For walkers who want long rails but also the option of a gentle jog as they get fitter.",
    description: "The Lastforever pairs full-length rails with a wider speed range than the other Amazon picks. The listing describes extended full-length handrails on both sides for continuous support, a 2.5 HP motor with a speed range of 0.5 to 7.5 mph, a 41.3 by 16.5-inch five-layer belt with cushioning, a 310 lb maximum user weight on a reinforced frame, a large LED display, controls and heart-rate sensors on the handrails so you can adjust the pace without bending, 12 preset programs, app control, transport wheels, a manual lubrication system, and a one-year warranty. The 7.5 mph top speed is the reason to choose it: it lets a walker progress to a light jog without changing machines. Keep that in proportion, though. A 41.3-inch belt is short for running, so any jog should be easy and compact, and the 0.5 mph starting speed is a little brisker than the 0.3 mph of the Exerpeutic and Redliro. The 310 lb rating is lower than those two as well. For a walker who expects to want more speed, it is a good balance. Amazon listed it at $399.99 on 6 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "yesoul-treadmill-for-seniors",
    name: "Yesoul Treadmill for Seniors",
    brand: "Yesoul",
    category: "Best Budget Treadmill With Handrails",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FRMGHZG5?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
